{
  "schema_version": 1,
  "id": "lt-morales",
  "name": "Lt. Morales",
  "role": "Healer",
  "overview": "Lt. Morales is a powerful single-target Healer who can provide Armor to allied Heroes, but her lack of mobility and crowd control makes her an easy target to engage on, especially if you are not careful with her positioning.",
  "strengths": [
    "Powerful single-target heals via Healing Beam and damage reduction via Safeguard",
    "Ability to interrupt any stationary-channeled Ability using Displacement Grenade",
    "Synergy with marksmen thanks to Stim Drone",
    "Team-wide global with Medivac Dropships"
  ],
  "weaknesses": [
    "Lack of area of effect healing",
    "Healing Beam is quite Energy consuming",
    "Almost non-existent crowd control",
    "No mobility",
    "Low self-healing",
    "No access to Cleanse or similar tools to remove crowd-control effects",
    "Unable to provide Unstoppable frames"
  ],
  "synergies": {
    "heroes": [
      {
        "id": "johanna",
        "name": "Johanna"
      },
      {
        "id": "raynor",
        "name": "Raynor"
      }
    ],
    "explanation": "Lt. Morales requires a solid Tank who can consistently peel multiple enemy Heroes away from her (such as E.T.C.). If you want to get value from Stim Drone, you need a marksman in your team (for example Sgt. Hammer)."
  },
  "counters": {
    "heroes": [
      {
        "id": "garrosh",
        "name": "Garrosh"
      },
      {
        "id": "chen",
        "name": "Chen"
      },
      {
        "id": "chromie",
        "name": "Chromie"
      },
      {
        "id": "lunara",
        "name": "Lunara"
      },
      {
        "id": "auriel",
        "name": "Auriel"
      }
    ],
    "explanation": "Considering that Healing Beam needs the targeted allied Hero to be in range for the whole time and not just the moment you cast it, Lt. Morales suffers against Heroes who have Displacement effects (such as Garrosh and Junkrat). Due to her limited self-healing and lack of crowd control, she does not like to play against dive compositions that count on aggressive Heroes who can directly engage on her by skipping her frontline (for example Zeratul and Anub'arak). What is often overlooked is the fact that she suffers poke damage because it can drain out her Energy in around 20 seconds, something that will make her almost useless for a while. As a consequence of how her Energy works, she does not want to take prolonged fights, especially when the enemy team can get value out of them (such as Auriel). Last but not the least, she definitely suffers area of effect damage (for example Lunara) because all of her Abilities can heal or mitigate damage on a single allied Hero at a time."
  },
